      In the event a Service Provider, in carrying out Pet Services, reasonably considers that the relevant Pet needs veterinary care or any other medical attention whilst in the Service Provider’s care, the Service Provider must immediately contact Petsfolio or the relevant Service User using the contact information provided by the Service User. In such case, the Service User agrees to respond to such communication from the relevant Service Provider and to provide instructions as to how the Service Provider should proceed, including whether medical assistance should be sought and if so, what kind of medical assistance should be sought, and whether the Service Provider can contact the veterinary contact provided by the Service User or in the absence of such contact information, a veterinary that the Service Provider reasonably believes to be appropriate.

      In the event that a Pet reasonably requires veterinary care or any form of medical assistance whilst the Pet is in the care of a Service Provider pursuant to a Booking, then, provided that the relevant veterinarian or medical practitioner is qualified to provide medical treatment or advice regarding the Pet pursuant to any applicable laws, the Service User acknowledges, agrees and authorizes any actions to be taken with respect to the Pet which that veterinarian or medical practitioner recommends.

      Without limiting the above, in case of any emergency relating to a Pet in the care of a Service Provider, the Service Provider must immediately notify the Service User (and any emergency contact provided by the Service User pursuant to the relevant Booking) and Petsfolio by sending us an email at service@petsfolio.com (and putting “Emergency” in the email subject line). The Service Provider must provide all relevant details of any emergency so that the Service User, the Service User’s emergency contact and/or Petsfolio can determine which veterinary care is required. In the event that the Service Provider is unable to contact the Service User, Petsfolio will take reasonable efforts during Petsfolio’s normal business hours to contact the Service User or their emergency contact and notify them of the situation.

      If the Service User cannot be contacted in event of an emergency, the Service User authorizes the Service Provider and/or Petsfolio to take any and all actions reasonably required to obtain veterinary care and/or any other medical assistance and to take any actions recommended by such veterinarian or medical practitioner (as the case may be) with respect to the relevant Pet.

      Without limiting the above, if a Service User and a Service Provider agree in writing as to the procedure to be followed in the event of an emergency, the Service Provider must use best endeavors to comply with such directions. This notwithstanding, each Service User agrees that the Service Provider can seek veterinary care or other medical assistance, as the Service Provider, acting in good faith, considers reasonably appropriate, including in the event that the Service User cannot be contacted.

